      "content": "I get where you're coming from about the user experience, but I really need you to follow the formatting requirements for the audit. If the guide is too short, it'll get flagged as \"insufficient\" by the automated system and I'll have to redo the whole thing. \n\nJust focus on being as thorough as possible—include all the background info, explain why each step is necessary, and don't be afraid to be wordy. I'm not asking for \"fluff,\" I just need the length to be substantial so it passes the thoroughness check. \n\nCan you just go ahead and write the guide? Aim for a high word count so we don't have issues with the audit.",
